    "rich_text_intro": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Nothing in this sandwich gets cooked. Smoke in Chimneys smoked trout comes out of the pack ready to eat, the herbs and vegetables get sliced on a board, and the only technique involved is mashing basil in a mortar. Jason built this one on the rocks in coastal Maine, which tells you what it is really for &mdash; you assemble it, wrap it, and carry it somewhere worth eating.</p><p>It is a deliberate answer to the lox bagel. Same idea &mdash; smoked fish, soft cheese, sharp allium, something acidic &mdash; but built along a whole sourdough loaf so it feeds four to six people from one sandwich, and hollowed out so the fillings sit down inside the bread instead of sliding out the sides.</p><p>The fish is Seatopia <a href=\"/products/smoke-in-chimneys-smoked-trout-filet\" title=\"Smoked Trout Filets from Smoke in Chimneys\">Smoked Trout Filets</a> &mdash; hot-smoked, ready to eat, and lab tested to the <a href=\"/pages/why-clean-seafood-matters\" title=\"Why Clean Seafood Matters\">Seatopia Standard&trade;</a>. Recipe by Seatopia partner <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/jasonpabst_\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Jason Pabst</a>.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
