        "g_head": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Picked in the garden, built on the rocks",
            "heading_size": "title-md",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The scapes, basil, dill, tomatoes and lettuce in this sandwich came out of the garden in the first photo &mdash; a few dozen steps from where it got eaten. That is the whole argument for a no-cook recipe: when the produce is picked that morning, the less you do to it the better it tastes.</p><p>The one thing that cannot come from the garden is clean fish. Hot-smoked trout is the part we can promise for you &mdash; ready to eat, third-party tested, and stable in the freezer until the morning you want to carry a sandwich down to the water.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
