    "rich_text_standard": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "h_std": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Ready-to-eat fish you can actually trust",
            "heading_size": "title-sm",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "t_std": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Smoked fish is eaten straight from the pack, with no cooking step in between, which makes the testing matter more rather than less. The Smoke in Chimneys trout in this sandwich is third-party lab tested: mercury at <strong>0.0097 ppm</strong> &mdash; roughly a tenth of the 0.1 ppm ceiling of the Seatopia Standard &mdash; and <strong>no detectable microplastics</strong> across all six polymers screened.</p><p>It carries about <strong>18 g of protein per 100 g</strong>, and it is farmed in spring-fed raceways in Virginia rather than netted at sea. You can read exactly how we test on our <a href=\"/pages/seatopia-testing-commitment\" title=\"Seatopia's Testing Commitment\">testing commitment page</a>.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
